---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import SliderDemo from "../../components/SliderDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Slider"
  description="A track and thumb for picking a number or a range of numbers."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Slider</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A track with a draggable thumb. Use it to pick one number, such as a volume,
    or a range between two numbers.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><SliderDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Slider usage"
      code={`import { Slider } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/slider";

const [volume, setVolume] = useState(40);
const [range, setRange] = useState([20, 75]);

<Slider
  aria-label="Volume"
  value={volume}
  onValueChange={(next) => setVolume(typeof next === "number" ? next : next[0])}
/>

<Slider
  aria-label="Range"
  value={range}
  onValueChange={(next) => typeof next !== "number" && setRange([...next])}
/>

<Slider aria-label="Disabled" disabled defaultValue={65} />

<div className="h-48">
  <Slider aria-label="Vertical volume" orientation="vertical" defaultValue={60} />
</div>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass <code>value</code> and <code>onValueChange</code> to control the slider,
      or <code>defaultValue</code> to let it keep its own state. A number gets one
      thumb; an array gets one thumb per entry. With no value, the slider has one
      thumb at <code>min</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>min</code> defaults to <code>0</code> and <code>max</code> to
      <code>100</code>. <code>orientation</code> is
      <code>"horizontal"</code> (fills its parent's width) or
      <code>"vertical"</code> (fills its parent's height, at least 160px). The track
      is 4px thick and the thumb is 12px, kept inside the track ends.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>disabled</code> dims the slider to 50% and blocks input; a disabled
      <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> does the same. The slider also takes Base UI props
      such as <code>step</code>, <code>largeStep</code>,
      <code>minStepsBetweenValues</code>, <code>name</code>,
      <code>format</code>, <code>onValueCommitted</code>, and state functions
      for <code>className</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Each thumb is a range input. The root <code>aria-label</code> names the thumbs
      too; a range adds "minimum" and "maximum". Use
      <code>getAriaLabel</code> for other names, or
      <code>aria-labelledby</code> to point at visible text.
      <code>getAriaValueText</code> sets the spoken value.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tab moves between thumbs. Arrow keys move one <code>step</code>, Page Up
      and Page Down move one <code>largeStep</code>, and Home and End jump to
      the ends. Hover, drag, and keyboard focus show a 3px ring that fades in
      over 120ms; the fade stops when reduced motion is requested. In forced
      colors mode the track, range, and thumb use system colors.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The track uses <code>--sprout-input</code> and the filled range uses
      <code>--sprout-primary</code>, so the opt-in TulipFarm theme tints it
      green. The thumb is white with a <code>--sprout-focus</code> border and ring.
      Override <code>--sprout-slider-thumb</code> to change the thumb fill.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
